rue,"use_doc_unwarping":true},"angle":0}},"markdown":{"text":"Trepent references having been made to Mefo? Cantor Voo by Parties in the Mofussul, to know the terms on which they conduct agency Business, it has occurred to them that this information cannot be better conveyed than by a Circular, explaining shortly the rates of commis. soon, as well as the general plan they pursue, in the management of their Constituents affairs\n\nWith this view, the following statement has been prepared: I\n\nTo prevent as far as possible any misapprehension on the part of Constituents\n\nwhose attention may not have been directed to the subject. Mefs Lanto\n\nTo take the present opportunity to enclose it to all their correspondents.\n\nCommission on executing orders for Goods Vca _____ 5 per cent\n\non guarantee bills, and on becoming security\n\nfor Administration of Estate ___ 2/2 \"On Executionship ___ 5.\n\nOn management of estate for Executors __ 2/2\n\non effecting insurance on lives and property __/2.\n\nOn purchasing or negotiating Bills of\n\nExchange _____1.\n\nOn returned Bulls\n\nOn Collecting House Rent ___2½.\n\nOn granting letters of credit ___\n\nOn sale & purchase of Government Securities Transfer","images":{}},"outputImages":{"layout_det_res":"https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//79f78099-07c1-4b9c-9e5d-d57f8b339843/layout_det_res_0.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-31T10%3A10%3A28Z%2F-1%2F%2F5dcc64a56327cf2d1fdac763a8b0a6b66f1b52f11bace8d67227d78b73de1cdf"},"inputImage":"https://pplines-online.bj.bcebos.com/deploy/official/paddleocr/pp-ocr-vl-16-online//79f78099-07c1-4b9c-9e5d-d57f8b339843/input_img_0.jpg?authorization=bce-auth-v1%2FALTAKDN8mY5KlNI7zaRpLmOqrw%2F2026-08-31T10%3A10%3A28Z%2F-1%2F%2F9d247aadf557a2f5ac66113c8f2ff29e1bc9ab66007db169ed251db7586f958c"},{"prunedResult":{"model_settings":{"use_doc_preprocessor":true,"use_layout_detection":true,"use_chart_recognition":true,"use_seal_recognition":true,"use_ocr_for_image_block":true,"format_block_content":true,"merge_layout_blocks":true,"markdown_ignore_labels":["number","footnote","header","header_image","footer","footer_image","aside_text"],"return_layout_polygon_points":true},"parsing_res_list":[{"block_label":"text","block_content":"Directory; and are consequently adhered to by all the Agents in Calcutta.\n\nMets: Lantor Ho however, do not allow interest on money deposited with them. Her object is to assimilate pecuniary transactions to the practice of private Bankers in London. A system which experience has proved to be founded on sound principles. They neither require advances, nor do they wish to be put to any. Constituents are expected to provide the necessary funds for their orders; beyond this, Mets: Lantor Ho do not desire remittances; but if made, the money is at all times ready to be afflicted as directed.","block_bbox":[49,35,1189,653],"block_id":0,"block_order":1,"group_id":0,"block_polygon_points":[[49.0,35.0],[1189.0,35.0],[1189.0,653.0],[49.0,653.0]]},{"block_label":"text","block_content":"Mefs: Fanta or Correspond with the Banking House of\n\nMefs: Courts or Strand London: through whom all Recumary\n\nMatters (Letters of Credit included) are transacted. And Mefs:\n\nI Cockburn Ho No 11. Broad Street act as their Agents, for\n\nthe execution of Commissions, as well as the transmission of Packag\n\nBe to, and from England.","block_bbox":[47,655,1190,1091],"block_id":1,"block_order":2,"group_id":1,"block_polygon_points":[[47.0,655.0],[1191.0,655.0],[1191.0,1091.0],[47.0,1091.0]]},{"block_label":"text","block_content":"No-3 Fourhe Place balcutta","block_bbox":[18,1142,599,1221],"block_id":2,"block_order":3,"group_id":2,"block_polygon_points":[[18.0,1142.0],[599.0,1142.0],[599.0,1221.0],[18.0,1221.0]]},{"block_label":"text","block_content":"2/4 July 1834. S","block_bbox":[148,1224,608,1330],"block_id":3,"block_order":4,"group_id":3,"block_polygon_points":[[148.0,1224.0],[608.0